  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the following circuit, the magnitude of current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>, is ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0124_ca5dcb902e2c.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 312px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0124_66e599a6208c.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 328px;\" /></p><p>The figure above shows the current and voltage at different points in circuit.</p><p>Applying Kirchhoff&#39;s Junction law at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Applying Kirchhoff&#39;s Junction law at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Solving equation (1) and&nbsp;(2), we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now, at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;junction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.</p>"
  }
}